## Context
After ticket 0113 renamed `ticket.go` → `erg.go`, the file still mixes two
distinct types: `Erg` (ticket model) and `Ref` (cross-reference, local or forge).
The Ref code (lines 13-119) has no dependency on Erg and is logically separate:

- `RefKind` enum + constants
- `Ref` struct + `IsForge()` method
- `parseRef` parser
- `allDigits`, `validateIssueNumber` helpers

Splitting follows the Go convention: one dominant type per file.

## Actions
1. Create `src/go/ref.go` with `RefKind`, `Ref`, `IsForge()`, `parseRef`,
   `allDigits`, `validateIssueNumber`.
2. Remove those declarations from `erg.go`.
3. If any Ref tests live in `erg_test.go`, split them into `ref_test.go`.
4. Verify `make test` passes.

## Exit criteria
- `ref.go` contains all Ref-related code; `erg.go` contains only Erg-related code.
- No cross-file shared helpers were duplicated.
- `make test` passes.
